  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm {Lyman}$<br/><img src=\"assets\\st0000_899f3d9a898d.png\"/><br/>$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1}=\\mathrm{R}\\left[\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right]=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{R}}{4}$<br/>$\\lambda_1=\\frac{4}{3 R}$ ________...(1)<br/>and $\\mathrm {Balmer}$<img src=\"assets\\st0000_cb4b951beeab.png\"/><br/>$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_2}=\\mathrm{R}\\left[\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{9}\\right]=\\frac{5 \\mathrm{R}}{36}$<br/>$\\lambda_2=\\frac{36}{5 R}$<br/>Then, $\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_2}=\\frac{5}{27}$"
